 "result_text": "`github checkout-pr` now gives a different error for a closed PR than for one that doesn't exist. I only checked that the module imports. I didn't run the command or hit the GitHub API, and I added no tests.\n\nWhen the PR number isn't in the open-PR list, the code now makes a second request for that single PR (`GET /repos/{org}/{repo}/pulls/{number}`).\n\n- **Closed PR:** if its state is `closed`, the error is ``PR #204 is already closed in repository `org/repo` ``.\n- **Missing PR:** if the request fails (for example a 404), or the PR isn't closed, you get the original \"is not found\" message.\n\nThe new helper is `is_pull_request_closed` in `git_machete/github.py`. The check is in `checkout_github_prs` in `git_machete/client.py`.\n\nA merged PR also has state `closed` on GitHub, so it gets the \"already closed\" message too.",
